title: Party Agenda
subtitle: Organisational work, collections, the apparatus and cooperatives.
is-card: true
tags: party_affairs
view-if: {! return !!Q.S && !!Q.polish_party_rules && PolishParty.agendaAvailable(Q) !}
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
// The party's standing actions (technical reference 4.4, 13.1–13.2, 17.2; card catalogue 5.5–5.9): each costs this
// month's action; organisational work needs no money. Since Z — 0.57 (item 11 of the play notes of 5 X 2026) it is an
// ordinary card of the Party deck, no longer pinned: it has to be drawn and goes back to the hand unused. Z — 0.78 (decision 5A
// of 8 X 2026): the TUR courses have their own card, polish_party_tur; organisational work is two options straight on this page,
// the target picked by the game (decision 4A).
PolishParty.agendaView(Q);
// Stage 7: the assessment of the forces of the state is a standing action of this agenda (card catalogue 6.8).
if (Q.polish_security_rules && typeof PolishSecurity !== 'undefined' && PolishSecurity.ready(Q)) Q.pl_pa_assess_why = PolishSecurity.assessStatus(Q).reason;
!}

= The party agenda

Party money: [+ pl_party_cash +]. A collection brings [+ pl_pa_fundraise_gain +] R now.

TUR: [+ pl_party_tur +]. Cooperatives: [+ pl_party_coops +].

[? if pl_pa_priorities : Economic priorities of PPS: [+ pl_pa_priorities +]. Each is prepared through its government card, with its own costs. ?]

- @organize_unions
- @organize_voters
- @fundraise
- @apparatus
- @launch_cooperative
- @kpp_rules
- @kpp_agreement
- @assess_forces
- @easy_discard

@fundraise
title: An extraordinary collection
subtitle: Brings [+ pl_pa_fundraise_gain +] resources (dues × membership / 100, with the bonus of the apparatus); waits three months.
choose-if: {! return PolishParty.fundraiseStatus(Q).available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_pa_fundraise_why +]
on-arrival: {!
PolishParty.fundraise(Q);
!}
go-to: result

@apparatus
title: Build up the party apparatus
subtitle: 2 resources; one level more (up to 4): every collection brings more (+25% for each level above the first).
choose-if: {! return PolishParty.apparatusStatus(Q).available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_pa_apparatus_why +]
on-arrival: {!
PolishParty.buildApparatus(Q);
!}
go-to: result

@organize_unions
title: Organisational work in the unions
subtitle: No money. [+ pl_pa_org_unions_text +]
choose-if: {! return PolishParty.organizeStatusOf(Q, 'unions').available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_pa_org_unions_why +]
on-arrival: {!
PolishParty.organizeUnions(Q);
!}
go-to: result

@organize_voters
title: Organisational work among our voters
subtitle: No money; the groups of the character of the party. [+ pl_pa_org_voters_text +]
choose-if: {! return PolishParty.organizeStatusOf(Q, 'voters').available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_pa_org_voters_why +]
on-arrival: {!
PolishParty.organizeVoters(Q);
!}
go-to: result

@launch_cooperative
title: Launch the prepared cooperative
subtitle: This month's action and 2 resources: [+ pl_pa_coop_name +] starts work and gives relief while it operates.
view-if: pl_pa_coop_count > 0
choose-if: {! return PolishParty.cooperativeStatus(Q, Q.pl_pa_coop_id).available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_pa_coop_why +]
on-arrival: {!
PolishParty.launchCooperative(Q, Q.pl_pa_coop_id);
!}
go-to: result

# Stage 8 (fix 2): trials of joint action with the KPP are agreed in a strike, in its step of cooperation with the
# communists (14.3, 9.6), so this option is not on the agenda's list; the scene stays for the rule PolishParty.kppStep.
@kpp_trial
title: Cooperation with the KPP: agree on a trial
subtitle: This month's action; a trial of joint action for an existing demand, at a relation of 30 or more. Relation now [+ pl_kpp_relation +].
view-if: pl_pa_kpp_open = 1
choose-if: {! return PolishParty.kppStepStatus(Q, 'trial').available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_kpp_trial_why +]
on-arrival: {!
PolishParty.kppStep(Q, 'trial');
!}
go-to: result

@kpp_rules
title: Cooperation with the KPP: agree on the rules
subtitle: This month's action; after two different successful joint actions, one of them full, at a relation of 50 or more.
view-if: pl_pa_kpp_open = 1
choose-if: {! return PolishParty.kppStepStatus(Q, 'rules').available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_kpp_rules_why +]
on-arrival: {!
PolishParty.kppStep(Q, 'rules');
!}
go-to: result

@kpp_agreement
title: Cooperation with the KPP: a broader agreement
subtitle: This month's action and 1 resource; needs rules accepted by both sides and the acceptance of 60 inside PPS (now [+ pl_kpp_acceptance +]).
view-if: pl_pa_kpp_open = 1
choose-if: {! return PolishParty.kppStepStatus(Q, 'agreement').available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_kpp_agreement_why +]
on-arrival: {!
PolishParty.kppStep(Q, 'agreement');
!}
go-to: result

@assess_forces
title: Assess the forces of the state
subtitle: 1 resource; the known loyalty of the army groups becomes more precise (−10 percentage points of the interval, down to ±5); waits three months. The loyalties themselves do not change.
view-if: {! return !!Q.polish_security_rules && PolishSecurity.ready(Q) !}
choose-if: {! return PolishSecurity.assessStatus(Q).available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_pa_assess_why +]
on-arrival: {!
PolishSecurity.assess(Q);
Q.pl_party_result = Q.pl_security_result;
!}
go-to: result

@result
new-page: true

= The party agenda

[+ pl_party_result +]

- @root: Continue.
